<section id="insurance">
  <p class="lab">Medical cover</p>
  <div class="ins-head">
    <svg class="ins-motif" width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0E7A5F" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2a7 7 0 0 0-7 7c0 5 7 12 7 12s7-7 7-12a7 7 0 0 0-7-7z"/><path d="M12 6v6M9 9h6"/></svg>
    <h2>The one cost with no price tag.</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="sub">Every other number on this page has a price you can look up. This one does not, and it can be the largest of them all. Most US health plans cover little or nothing once you leave the country, and Medicare covers essentially none of it abroad. A serious illness or injury is paid up front, and a medical evacuation runs from tens of thousands of dollars to past $100,000 if you are remote or an ocean from home.</p>

  <div class="ins">
    <div class="ins-skip">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0A5644" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.5-7 9-4-1.5-7-4.5-7-9V6z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
      <div>
        <p class="ins-skip-h">First, you may not need to buy anything.</p>
        <p>A cheap, refundable trip close to home does not need this. And if you are healthy, headed somewhere with good care, and one of the premium cards on the shortlist above already includes emergency medical and evacuation, you may be covered already. Check your card's benefits guide before you buy. Saying that costs us the commission, and it is still the right call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ins-dial">
      <p class="ins-dlab">How much cover matters here</p>
      <div class="ins-gauge" data-level={insLevel} role="slider" tabindex="0"
        aria-label="How much cover matters here" aria-valuemin="1" aria-valuemax="3"
        aria-valuenow={insLevel === "low" ? 1 : insLevel === "medium" ? 2 : 3} aria-valuetext={insLevel}
        data-low={insLevels.low} data-medium={insLevels.medium} data-high={insLevels.high}>
        <div class="ins-track"><span class="ins-fill"></span><span class="ins-mark"></span></div>
